# Difficulty modes & dashboard

## Model
- **One game, three profiles** — never fork mission content/story for Easy/Hard.
- Profiles live in `web/lib/game/difficulty.ts`. `User.difficulty` (from invite/group) → mission page → `DifficultyProvider` → M1–M5 balances stamped on game state.
- **Standard** ≡ original shipped Medium. Easy/Hard are numeric dials only (detection, hints, M1 reconnects, M3 sign-off/catastrophic, M5 retries/framing).

## Easy (shipped baseline after review)
- Softer meter (~0.55× penalty, ~0.45× passive), cheaper hints, **2** M1 reconnects, M3 sign-off ≤**78%**, softer vault→public spike.
- M5 ships at **4/4** commits with **2** crew retries (not 3/4 — keep shared finale bar).
- Tutorial/protocol copy must use live profile numbers (no hardcoded “≤55%” / “+8%”).

## Hard
- Same wiring as Easy; profile: higher passive/penalty/hints, **0** M1 reconnects, M3 sign-off ≤**38%**, catastrophic via penalty only (no double-scale), M5 **4/4** with **1** crew retry, framing ~1.4×.
- Four-lens QA consensus: ease passive (~1.4×) and unstack M3 catastrophic + finale cliff; keep no M1 reconnect as Hard identity.
- Review/tune Hard with the same four lenses (analyst, student, designer, facilitator) before treating it as classroom-ready.

## Dashboard / invites (when working on maverxdashboard or invite APIs)
- Invite difficulty already flows: dashboard → invite → register redeem → `User.difficulty` / group.
- Keep invite labels Easy / Standard / Hard aligned with `difficultyNormalize` and profile ids.
- Do **not** invent a separate difficulty system in the dashboard; it only selects the profile the game already applies.
- Prefer cohort-wide one difficulty per room (mixed Easy+Standard in one debrief muddies win badges).
- Still open: persist difficulty on mission reports/analytics so Easy vs Hard completions are distinguishable.

